  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nFor the remainder of the weekend and into early next week we remain \nin a weakness between high pressure to the northwest and high \npressure to the east. With this we will keep a low chance of rain as \nbits of energy and some elevated moisture work toward the Texas \ncoast. Mainly we're looking at a few sea breeze showers and storms, \nbut some morning convection will also be possible along the coast \nwithin some marginal instability. Beyond Monday the ridge to the \nnorthwest begins to collapse and the ridge east shifts move over the \nregion limiting rain chances for the rest of the week. \n\nTemperatures remain generally around seasonal averages, but will \nrange from a degree or two below normal Sunday to a few degrees \nabove normal by late in the work week. Heat index values increase \nfor the latter half of the period and heat advisories may become \nnecessary by mid-week.",
